---
import CodeBlock from '../ui/CodeBlock.astro';
import AggregationPlan from './AggregationPlan.astro';
import SQLExample from './SQLExample.astro';
import ChapterOrnament from './ChapterOrnament.astro';
import { crossfieldDocs, jaffleExplainSQL } from '../../data/crossfield';
import capture from '../../../public/crossfield/jaffle-explain-semantic.json';
---
<section class="explanation" id="inspect-sql" aria-labelledby="explanation-heading">
  <div class="explain-intro">
    <div>
      <ChapterOrnament section="retail-calculation" />
      <h2 id="explanation-heading">Review how each result is calculated.</h2>
      <p>The store report combines revenue from orders with a count of receipt lines. Crossfield calculates each measure independently before joining the results by store. Reviewers can inspect that aggregation strategy in the generated SQL.</p>
      <p><code>EXPLAIN (SEMANTIC)</code> shows the selected definitions and generated SQL without executing the report or calling providers. This gives reviewers an explicit record of the calculation before execution.</p>
      <a class="explain-link" href={`${crossfieldDocs}/discovery#inspect-semantic-intent`}>How to inspect a semantic query →</a>
    </div>
    <AggregationPlan />
  </div>
  <div class="explanation-code">
    <SQLExample summary="Inspect the semantic query" purpose="This request asks Crossfield to explain the retail report. It demonstrates how a reviewer can inspect the calculation without running the report.">
      <CodeBlock code={jaffleExplainSQL} title="SQL · Explain the store report" tryable={false} />
    </SQLExample>
    <SQLExample summary="Read the complete generated SQL" purpose="This is the captured engine expansion behind the diagram. Look for the separate order and receipt-line aggregates, followed by their joins at the store dimension.">
      <CodeBlock code={capture.expanded_sql} title="expanded_sql · Complete captured output" tryable={false} />
    </SQLExample>
  </div>
  <p class="capture-note">Captured from the matching build and <a href={`${crossfieldDocs}/quickstart`}>retail fixture</a>. <a href="/crossfield/jaffle-expanded.sql" download>Download the SQL</a> · <a href="/crossfield/jaffle-explain-semantic.json" download>Download the full explanation as JSON</a>. Generated aliases are not stable identities.</p>
  <p class="capture-note">Execute the original semantic query to retain Crossfield’s validation. <code>EXPLAIN (SQL)</code> also binds and optimizes; binding can invoke provider callbacks. <code>EXPLAIN ANALYZE</code> executes.</p>
</section>
<style>
  .explanation { padding-block: 4.5rem; scroll-margin-top: 9rem; }
  .explain-intro { display: grid; gap: 2.5rem; align-items: center; }
  .explain-intro > * { min-width: 0; }
  h2 { margin-top: 0; font-size: clamp(2rem,3.5vw,3rem); line-height: 1.15; }
  p { margin-block: 1rem; color: var(--color-soil-700); font-size: 1rem; line-height: 1.8; }
  p code { font-size: .85em; }
  .explain-link { color: var(--color-field-700); text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 4px; font-size: .875rem; }
  .explanation-code { margin-top: 2rem; }
  .capture-note { font-size: .8rem; }
  .capture-note a { color: var(--color-link); text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 3px; }
  @media(min-width:1024px) { .explain-intro { grid-template-columns: minmax(0,1fr) minmax(0,1fr); gap: 4rem; } }
  @media(max-width:640px) { .explanation { padding-block: 3rem; } }
</style>
